<template>
  <main class="site-frame py-10 md:py-16">
    <section class="hero-orbit rounded-[2rem] p-7 text-white md:p-12">
      <p class="eyebrow !text-sky-300">Optional single-file authoring</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-black tracking-tight md:text-6xl">One file when co-location improves clarity.</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-slate-300">
        A <code>.vd</code> file keeps template, behavior, styles, and config
        together for a small page or component. Folder mode remains the default
        for a feature that is likely to grow.
      </p>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary mt-7 rounded-xl" vd-on:click="increment()">
        Live count: {{ count }}
      </button>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_.9fr]">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">The complete module</p>
        <h2 class="section-heading mt-3">A `.vd` file compiles to the same internal resource shape.</h2>
        <p class="section-copy">The compiler requires one template block. Script, style, and config blocks are optional and use the same public contracts as the folder files.</p>
        <div class="code-window">
          <div class="code-toolbar"><span>src/pages/about.vd</span><span>template + script + style + config</span></div>
          <pre class="code-example" vd-pre><code>&lt;template&gt;
  &lt;main&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;{{ title }}&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;button vd-on:click="count++"&gt;Count: {{ count }}&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;/main&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
export const state = { title: "About", count: 0 };
&lt;/script&gt;

&lt;style&gt;
main { padding: 2rem; }
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;config&gt;
export default { path: "/about", seo: { title: "About" } };
&lt;/config&gt;</code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside class="space-y-5">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="badge badge-primary badge-outline">Same compiler</span>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-black text-slate-950">No alternate runtime.</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Folder mode and one-file mode create the same template, script, style, config, and source resource. Choosing `.vd` does not disable routing, SEO, components, or scoped styles.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="badge badge-primary badge-outline">One source of truth</span>
          <h2 class="mt-4 text-xl font-black text-slate-950">Choose one layout per feature.</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600">Do not create both a folder resource and a same-named `.vd` resource. VeloDom reports ambiguity instead of choosing silently.</p>
        </article>
        <a href="/features#pages" vd-nav class="btn btn-outline w-full rounded-xl">Compare with folder pages</a>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </main>
</template>

<script>
export function init({ state }) {
  state.count = 0;
  state.increment = () => {
    state.count += 1;
  };
}
</script>

<style>
main code:not(pre code) {
  border-radius: 0.375rem;
  background: rgb(15 23 42 / 0.08);
  padding: 0.1rem 0.35rem;
}
</style>

